	(text_box "ToDo's:\n- add Silk Screen Labels for Qs and ~{Q}s on each IC pin\n- adjust via hole from Posts to tight fit\n- Name Sheets proper\n- estimate current\n- Overthink the purpose of B+\n- make long holes to holes to save space\n- add very small MLCCs to each Mosfet agains ringing\n- add series R and ESD Diodes to Dip Switch IC Gates\nDC/DC:\n- add TVS Diodes on the Flip Flops Inputs\n- add TVS Diode for the Mosfets Protection:\n  - TVS diode's breakdown voltage (VBR) must be higher than your normal operating voltage\n  - TVS diode's clamping voltage (VC) must be lower than the MOSFET's 30V maximum rating\n  - select a TVS diode with a clamping voltage (VC) of less than 30V\n  - 16V or 18V unidirectional TVS diode\n- is the 2kV C on the isolated power lines really needed?\n- add 1MR Minimelf parallel to the isolated grounds\n- EMI Filter\n\n#################################################\n- Qs re numbering -> done\n- switch to 4x D-Flip Flop wit Q and ~{Q} -> done\n- use fixed quarz oszi with 32 kHz -> done\n- use 4x D-Flip to devide down -> done\n- exchange to 4x SPDT switch to change clock and DIR -> done\n- add header and extra optocoupler for Tacho Out with V_{IN}\n  -> w Signal, from active clock signal (Clock_{RSR}) -> done\n- add two Ground Posts for the Osci Clip  -> done\n- seperate opto supply to buffered DC/DC In Voltage -> done\n- create a solder Jumper that is soldered during reflow and\n  put it between Power Supplys, instead or Zero Ohms -> done\n- exchange MosFet driver with dual ones in BGA package -> done\n- buffered 12V Voltage supplys VCCA/VCCB of MosFet drivers LOGIC -> done\n- checking if AND can be replaced with NANDs\n  -> not possible/available -> done\n- exchange SD103ASDM-7-F or rather remove it from the VDDA Path -> done\n- check if Ground is missing on VDDI input side GND1 -> done\n- reduce to one pcb, idealy only on top side -> done\n- switch two Mosfets of the same kind at once to save more space -> done\n- series resistors for all outputs -> done\nDC/DC:\n- remove Elko and add 10-20 22uF Cs to this supply -> done\n- exchange power supply to 5V LDO and dual voltage regulator for\n  negative supply -3.3V und +3.3V -> done\n- adjust undervoltage lockouts to 4V -> done\n- 3V3 from DC/DC supply to VDDI on MosFet drivers -> done\n- adjust L to 10µH -> done\n- check and add isolated DC/DC to seperate MosFet from Logic\n- 3V3 remove redundant Cs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
